Task: Performance benchmark (Phase 5, cmc-2d_20261025)

Measured CMC.mitigate latency over the 2-D synthetic search box for
N in {64,128,256} points per axis and 2/3/4 xApps (median of 3 runs after
warm-up, ANN surrogates, random_state=42, xApp grid 24, training excluded).

Results (ms): N=64 -> 1.6/2.3/3.0; N=128 -> 4.4/5.9/7.6;
N=256 -> 25.3/40.2/61.0. Default N=128 with 4 xApps is ~7.6 ms, well within
the 1 s scheduling budget.

Files:
- docs/usage/RUNNING_CMC.md

Why: NFR-4 requires demonstrating the default 2-D sweep fits the Near-RT-RIC
budget; the table also justifies the existing MAX_GRID_POINTS guard.
